# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Reproduces the resize path after #4566 (#4522's first
# fix) and before its resize fix (#4629): the resize mirror forwards a prepare
# as a plain write that R re-mints at its own clock, so a saga bound to T that
# prepares after the flip leaves buckets on R stamped below P and R's leaf
# clocks never see P. Once R splits, a later write on the split destination is
# stamped above the re-minted value but below P, and the terminal's
# committed-values backstop, carried at P, overwrites it. A clock merge at the
# flip does not help, because the saga prepared after it. The edits lie in
# BVal and KnowsP, the operators the read gate, the drain and the later write's
# stamp use, so the mutation declares no PERTURBS.
MODULE: NoKeyLostResizeMirrorUnmarkedPrepare
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the resize mirror re-mints a prepare at R's clock, so a later write on R is stamped below P and the backstop overwrites it

--- FIND
BVal(c) == SagaV
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a bucket the mirror forwards to R is re-minted at R's own clock.
BVal(c) == IF c = R /\ bound # R THEN SagaUV ELSE SagaV
--- END

--- FIND
KnowsP(c, s) == \E k \in Keys : Stamp(row[c][s][k]) >= Stamp(SagaV) \/ pend[c][s][k] # "none"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: such a bucket does not raise R's leaf clock to P.
KnowsP(c, s) == \E k \in Keys : Stamp(row[c][s][k]) >= Stamp(SagaV) \/ ((c = T \/ bound = R) /\ pend[c][s][k] # "none")
--- END